# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry, except
#                                  that a script named *acceptance*.bash may exit 2 for
#                                  COULD NOT ESTABLISH, as an acceptance.bash may
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00185 Task 1.1 (#60, wrong emoji glyphs): TRIAGE ONLY, READ-ONLY. The plan has only
# triage.bash; it changes nothing on the host, needs no sudo and never prompts. It records the
# terminal it runs in and every running terminal emulator (version, start time), the VTE
# version, the emoji font packages and their install times, fc-match and fc-list for the
# issue's code points, the fontconfig cache ages, which emoji font file each running terminal
# has mapped, and the terminals' font and GPU settings. Start meta-deploy from the terminal that
# draws the wrong emoji, and leave that window open while it runs.
00185-terminal-emoji-glyphs
# play-basic-configs.yml (no plan owns it): fwupd now runs LAST in the play, so every task before
# it applies even while LVFS's signature file (firmware.xml.zst.jcat) is unavailable; the fwupd
# task itself still fails (after its retries) until LVFS recovers. The run also rebuilds and
# installs the fetch-age command with Plan 00183's fix and applies the tasks that stopped behind
# fwupd before (the ABRT policy onward). It imports play-golang.yml first, so this is also the
# Go 1.26.10 toolchain run: golang is upgraded to Fedora's newest build (state latest) and the
# play fails unless `go env GOVERSION` is at least 1.26.10. play-golang.yml has no entry of its
# own: every play below imports it too.
playbooks/imports/play-basic-configs.yml
# play-agent-bus.yml, the whole play (Plan 00213's LXC fix, the farewell-reason fix, Plan 00211
# Phase 2's admin tool). BEFORE starting meta-deploy, restart every team's agent sessions, ccy
# and LXC alike, so each coordinator runs pingbus 0.2.0 (deploy 1 installed it; a running
# session keeps the pingbus it started with, and an old one rejects its questions invite): this
# play's team step runs `agent-bus bootstrap` for every team, which now creates each team's
# reports room, and its questions room when it has a coordinator, and invites you and the
# coordinators. The play rebuilds the host's pingbus.pyz and the member kit, so pingbus
# refuses a list or object farewell reason instead of crashing, and re-runs the member kit step
# (README.lxc step 1) for every LXC member: each member's copy of pingbus names that member's
# own newest Python 3.11 or later (the last run stopped there with exit 78 on an EL9 member,
# whose /usr/bin/python3 is 3.9, before replacing anything). A member with no Python 3.11 or
# later fails the play, naming what to install. It also builds the Go pingbus-status-line into
# the kit (used by the 00213 deploy below). Teams are not restarted unless the Tuwunel pin or
# the units changed, which this does not do. Needs sudo.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00213 Tasks 1.3, 1.4 and 2.3 (the bus status line in Go): deploy.bash runs the whole
# play-agent-bus.yml again (no change after the entry above), then the whole
# play-claude-yolo.yml, then acceptance.bash. The kit's settings.json runs the static Go
# pingbus-status-line, copied into every running LXC member. The ccy play gives the host CCY
# 3.99.13.11 and puts the binary in the image's build context (container 2.78.11, rebuilt once
# at the next ccy launch; the image also carries the farewell-reason fix, the reports and
# questions admin tool and Go 1.26.10 in the project image): a seated session's status line is
# the Go one and refreshes every 25 s. The acceptance checks the kit's, the image's and each
# declared LXC member's binary are this checkout's build (a declared container that is down is
# refused, named), runs the recorded Python goldens against the installed Python and Go, and
# measures the CPU one render costs in each: Go must cost under a fifth (the report has the
# figures). Needs sudo once. Afterwards restart the teams' agent sessions; a running one keeps
# its old status line.
00213-agent-bus-performance-go-carve-out/deploy.bash
# Plan 00211 deploy 2 (Task 2.6), the reports and questions rooms, LAST. It needs every team's
# agent sessions restarted first, ccy and LXC alike, so each coordinator runs pingbus 0.2.0 (see
# the play-agent-bus.yml entry above: restart them before meta-deploy starts). This runs
# deploy.bash --stage 2: it refuses unless the spike report says every fact holds, then runs
# acceptance.bash --stage 1 again as the pre-flight (the host's and every declared LXC
# member's pingbus is 0.2.0, and a declared container that is down is refused, named). Then the
# whole play-agent-bus.yml keeps each team's reports and questions rooms (created by the entry
# above), the index and the invites; the whole play-claude-yolo.yml finds the ccy image already
# at container 2.78.11. Then acceptance.bash --stage 2 waits up to 180 s for every coordinator
# to join its questions room and every running ccy seat its reports room, naming any that has
# not, and checks the rooms. It finds the first team's coordinator in its running ccy session
# or LXC member; with no team coordinator, or one whose session is not running, it is
# REJECTED, named, before it changes anything. It adds and removes one throwaway worker that
# must be refused the questions room and whose test report must reach no inbox, posts a second
# test report from inside an LXC member when one is declared (else it says that check was not
# judged), and has the coordinator ask a test question. Needs sudo once. Afterwards do the
# Element steps of the plan's ACCEPTANCE-owner.md.
00211-agent-bus-reports-and-questions-rooms/deploy-stage-2.bash
# Plan 00201 Task 2.7 (M7): the automated two-team acceptance again, because its M3 check
# (the session's status line) changed since it last passed, and Plan 00213's cut-over made
# that status line the Go one. acceptance.bash only: it makes two throwaway teams declared
# in a run-directory host_vars (your host_vars and teams are never touched), runs one headless
# ccy session on both and a plain one (each one short turn on haiku), checks descriptions,
# launch block, per-session record, status line, `say` and SessionEnd, then purges both teams
# and checks their firewalld rules are gone, however the run ends. Needs sudo once, ccy
# launched interactively in this checkout once (Quick Launch), and the hooks daemon installed.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker
# play-claude-yolo.yml, the whole play (Plan 00191 Tasks 4.3 and 4.4): the host's ccy becomes
# CCY 3.99.13.14. lib/tmux-session.bash no longer carries the unused bash take-over (taking a
# session over stays the ccy-sessions picker's Ctrl-T); the new lib/host-paths.bash lets the
# launcher's differential harness point the build context, GPU directory and zone database
# elsewhere (unset, nothing changes) and refuses a bad override at start; the launcher's
# temporary files follow TMPDIR when it is set. The image is unchanged at container 2.78.11,
# so no rebuild. It also rebuilds ~/.local/bin/ccy-teams with Plan 00209 stage 1 (the team,
# seat and declare reads in-process), which the check below judges. Afterwards start a ccy
# session as usual: it must start and attach as before.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00209 stage 1 host check, after the play-claude-yolo.yml entry above has installed the
# ccy-teams that reads team, seat and declare state in-process. READ-ONLY: it changes nothing,
# and keeps two builds and every output in its run directory. It checks the installed ccy-teams
# is this checkout's build, builds the ccy-teams from before stage 1 from git, and runs each three
# times in turn: `--list` must print the same bytes (a difference in every round rejects, one in
# some rounds only is a live change and a note) and run faster (it took 9-23 s before), and an
# open, drawn on this terminal and answered with Esc at its first screen, must be faster and
# start exactly one declare status and no agent-bus seat list. A live member.json that sets
# report_per_hour must be listed, not refused. Needs sudo once (so both read the member rosters)
# and a terminal. A failure names the check, and a --list diff is in the report. An open that
# asks a question first (a team to describe, an update) leaves S3 NOT JUDGED (exit 2, COULD NOT
# ESTABLISH in the summary): answer it in ccy-teams and run again. An out-of-date team is offered
# its update on every open, so it blocks S3 until play-agent-bus.yml has applied it; its entry
# above normally has.
00209-agent-bus-v2-in-go/acceptance-s1.bash
